The implementation compiles cleanly. When `ring` is asserted, the motor is enabled in vibrate mode and the ringer otherwise, ensuring exactly one output is active; when `ring` is low, both outputs are off.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  wire ring,
    input  wire vibrate_mode,
    output wire ringer,
    output wire motor
);

    assign ringer = ring & ~vibrate_mode;
    assign motor  = ring &  vibrate_mode;

endmodule
```
